{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.DeltaSkeinSubstrateIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.DeltaSkeinSubstrateIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.deltaSkeinTilde","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.deltaSkeinTilde","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/delta-skein-substrate-identity.lean#L74-L80","doc":"Per-Borromean-quantum dimensionless residual.\nDivides the Skein difference by the Borromean topological quantum\n`Vol(B_3)/ℏ_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.delta_skein_eq_mass_splitting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.delta_skein_eq_mass_splitting","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/delta-skein-substrate-identity.lean#L40-L72","doc":"Substrate identity for ΔS(n − p), conditional on the\ncommon-scale hypothesis.\n\nUnder [BorromeanCommonScale] (i.e. λ_scale is a single value\nshared between proton and neutron Borromean baryons), the\nproton–neutron mass splitting in units of m_e equals the\nSkein-difference of the orientation partitions:\n\n    m_n − m_p\n    ─────────  =  S(neutron) − S(proton)  =  ΔS(n − p).\n       m_e\n\nCombined with CODATA `m_n − m_p = Q_β + m_e`, this yields the\nclosed-form prediction\n\n    ΔS(n − p)  =  (Q_β + m_e) / m_e\n\nin CAL-1 (m_e) + CAL-3 (Q_β) only.  The 50-dps numerical\nwitness `m-baryon-volume-form.witness.json` confirms agreement\nto 1015 ppm vs the direct Kauffman-bracket evaluation of\n`skeinContribution(neutron) − skeinContribution(proton)` at q₀.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] Borromean baryon mass formula, common-scale\nSkein-difference identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.deltaMassOverMe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.deltaMassOverMe","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/delta-skein-substrate-identity.lean#L34-L38","doc":"The proton–neutron mass splitting in units of m_e.\nConventional CODATA identity Q_β = m_n − m_p − m_e gives\n(m_n − m_p) / m_e = (Q_β + m_e) / m_e. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.hbarQSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.hbarQSq","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/delta-skein-substrate-identity.lean#L31-L32","doc":"ℏ_q² for convenience. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/delta-skein-substrate-identity.lean#L27-L29","doc":"q-deformed Planck constant ℏ_q = (q − 1)/q.  Local copy\n(same provenance note as `volBorromean` above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Borromean.volBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Borromean.volBorromean","kind":"def","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/delta-skein-substrate-identity.lean#L19-L25","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Borromean rings complement.\nLocal copy of the constant defined in\n`borromean-baryon-mass-formula.lean` so this file elaborates\nstandalone (per Copilot review on PR #640 line 60).  Future\nconsolidation: move to a shared `QOU.Borromean.Constants`\nmodule. ","signatureChunk":0}]}